📘 Digitizers and Touchscreens

1. What is a Digitizer?

  - Converts analog touch/pen input into digital signals
  - Found in touchscreens, drawing tablets, stylus devices
  - Essential for graphic design, note-taking, professional use

2. Touchscreen Types

  - Type	Technology	Multi-Touch	Best For
  - Capacitive	Conductive layer Yes (pinch-to-zoom)	Smartphones, tablets, modern laptops
  - Resistive	Pressure-sensitive No (single-touch)	ATMs, industrial, gloves/any object
  - Infrared/SAW	Specialized	Varies	Specialized applications

3. Stylus Types

  - Type	Features	Use Case
  - Active	Pressure-sensitive, internal electronics	Digital art, drawing
  - Passive	No pressure sensitivity, like finger touch	General navigation
  - EMR	Electromagnetic resonance, high accuracy	Professional graphics tablets

4. Common Touchscreen Issues

  - Problem	Solution
  - Unresponsive screen	Restart, clean, update drivers, recalibrate
  - Ghost touches	Recalibrate or check for physical damage
  - Stylus not recognized	Check battery, update firmware/drivers
  - Delayed response	Overheating, insufficient memory, driver conflict
